# AI-signals pipeline working files live in data/, never in public/ — Vite copies
# public/ into dist, so anything there is published on the live site.
# These are per-run artifacts, regenerated each run.
# Globs, not exact paths: sector runs suffix the filename with the work dimension
# (data/_finder-rejected-worker-experience-identity-and-wellbeing.json), and this
# repo is public — the rejected list names stories the editorial team declined.
# (data/_seen-ledger.jsonl is committed state and is intentionally NOT ignored.)
data/_candidates*.json
data/_finder-output*.json
data/_finder-rejected*
data/_finder-report*.md

# Human review rationale: one event per accept/reject, carrying free-text
# judgment about named vendors, publications and individual practitioners.
# Same rule as the finder's rejection lists above, and for the same reason —
# this repo is public, and "SEO content with no method" attached to a named
# author does not belong in a permanent public history. The seen-ledger IS
# committed but records no reasons, which is why it can be.
#
# The cost: this file is local to one machine, so it is not shared between
# reviewers. That is the clearest pressure toward a private store — see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-12-source-profiles-and-review-log-design.md
data/_review-log.jsonl

# Source nominations awaiting review, and the accepted/ and rejected/ folders
# the reviewer moves them into. Unreviewed material naming individuals, on a
# public repo, plus a reviewer's reasons for declining a named person. Same rule
# as the two above.
#
# Note the cost, which bites hardest here: rejected/ is the memory that stops
# the loop re-nominating someone already declined, and that memory is local to
# one machine. Its value grows over time, which makes this the third and
# sharpest argument for a private store.
data/source-nominations/

# Staged signal drafts awaiting review, and the accepted/ and rejected/ folders
# the reviewer moves them into. Local scratch: this repo is public, and a draft
# is by definition unreviewed. Only what `signals:promote` moves into
# public/content/ai-signals/ is ever committed.
data/signal-drafts/

# Radar pipeline working files. Same rule as the finder artifacts above: data/ is
# never published, and this repo is public — a proposal is unreviewed research
# claims, and the reach log records how a reviewer judged them.
data/_radar-*

# Brainstorming mockups (visual companion scratch space) and the implementation-ledger directory
.superpowers/

# Left behind by browser automation tooling (Playwright MCP)
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code session state. Note .claude/worktrees/ holds *git worktrees* —
# full checkouts of this repo. Without this rule `git add -A` commits them as
# embedded git repositories, and ESLint lints them as if they were source,
# which reports every finding several times over.
.claude/

# The CI deployment tree: the production build with the preview build nested at
# preview/, assembled by deploy.yml and pushed to gh-pages in one go. Created
# locally only when rehearsing that sequence by hand.
_site

